      "text": "Svāgatasūtra",
      "segment_number": 1,
      "translated_text": "<s>Svāgatasūtra</s> (The Sūtra of Welcome)"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "1",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "śrāvast",
          "segment_number": 3,
          "translated_text": "In <s>Śrāvast</s>-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "y",
          "segment_number": 4,
          "translated_text": "-ī"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "āṃ",
          "segment_number": 5,
          "translated_text": "[continued]"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "/",
          "segment_number": 6,
          "translated_text": "/"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881r1: ///",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "bha",
              "segment_number": 8,
              "translated_text": "The Bles-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "gavāṃ śr",
              "segment_number": 9,
              "translated_text": "-sed One in <s>Śrā</s>-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "āva",
              "segment_number": 10,
              "translated_text": "-vast"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "styāṃ viharati sma je",
              "segment_number": 11,
              "translated_text": "-ī was dwelling in <s>Jeta</s>-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "tavane",
              "segment_number": 12,
              "translated_text": "-<s>vana</s>"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "///",
              "segment_number": 13,
              "translated_text": "[lacuna]"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 7,
          "translated_text": "[Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881r1: ///]"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 2,
      "translated_text": "1"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "2 svāga",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "taṃ vo bhikṣavaḥ / supravrajyā vo bhikṣavaḥ / lābhā sulabdhā",
          "segment_number": 15,
          "translated_text": "-ome to you, O <s>bhikṣus</s> (monks)! Well gone forth are you, O <s>bhikṣus</s>! The gains are well gained."
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "/ kadācit karh",
          "segment_number": 16,
          "translated_text": "At some time or"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "i",
          "segment_number": 17,
          "translated_text": "an-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "cid āryāyatane pratyājāti indriyair avik",
          "segment_number": 18,
          "translated_text": "-other, rebirth in a noble realm occurs — completeness of faculties, freedom from dull-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "alatā ajaḍatā aneḍamūkatā ahastasaṃvācakatā pratibalatā subhā",
          "segment_number": 19,
          "translated_text": "-ness, freedom from being mute and deaf, freedom from communicating only by hand gestures, the ability to understand the meaning of well-spoken and ill-spoken"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "ṣitadurbhāṣitānāṃ dharmāṇām artham ājñātum /",
          "segment_number": 20,
          "translated_text": "<s>dharmas</s> (teachings). /"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881r2: ///",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "svā",
              "segment_number": 22,
              "translated_text": "\"Welc-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "gataṃ vo",
              "segment_number": 23,
              "translated_text": "-ome to you,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "bhi",
              "segment_number": 24,
              "translated_text": "O <s>bhik</s>-"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "kṣavaḥ supravrajyaṃ su",
              "segment_number": 25,
              "translated_text": "-<s>ṣus</s>! Well gone forth, well"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "labdhā",
              "segment_number": 26,
              "translated_text": "gained,\""
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "///; r3: /// + .. indriyair avikalatā aja",
              "segment_number": 27,
              "translated_text": "[///; r3: /// + .. completeness of faculties, freedom from dull-]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "ḍatā",
              "segment_number": 28,
              "translated_text": "[-ness]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "+ ///; SBhV II 209.8-12: svāgataṃ vo bhikṣavaḥ supravrajitaṃ (MS °to); sulabdho vo manuṣyapratilambhaḥ; kadācit karhicid āryāyatane pratyājātiḥ, indriyair avikalatā, ajaḍatā, aneḍamūkatā, ahastasaṃvācikatā, pratibalatā subhāṣitadurbhāṣitānāṃ dharmāṇām artham ājñātuṃ",
              "segment_number": 29,
              "translated_text": "[+ ///; SBhV II 209.8-12: \"Welcome to you, O <s>bhikṣus</s>! Well gone forth! Well obtained is your human rebirth! At some time or another, rebirth in a noble realm occurs — completeness of faculties, freedom from dullness, freedom from being mute and deaf, freedom from communicating only by hand gestures, the ability to understand the meaning of well-spoken and ill-spoken <s>dharmas</s>.\"]"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 21,
          "translated_text": "[Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881r2: ///]"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 14,
      "translated_text": "2 \"Welc-"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "3 ahaṃ caitarhi śāstā loke utpannas tathāgato 'rhāṃ samyaksaṃbuddho vidyācaraṇasaṃpannaḥ sugato lokavid anuttara puruṣadamyasārathiḥ śāstā devamanuṣyāṇāṃ buddho bhagavāṃ /",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "blue"
          },
          "text": "Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881v1: ///",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "loka",
              "segment_number": 32,
              "translated_text": "Knower of the"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "vid anuttaraḥ puruṣadamyasārathi",
              "segment_number": 33,
              "translated_text": "world, unsurpassed charioteer of persons to be tamed,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "hi",
              "attributes": {
                "rend": "it"
              },
              "text": "ḥ",
              "segment_number": 34,
              "translated_text": "[continued]"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "///",
              "segment_number": 35,
              "translated_text": "[lacuna]"
            }
          ],
          "segment_number": 31,
          "translated_text": "[Cf. SHT IV (additions) 881v1: ///]"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 30,
      "translated_text": "3 \"And I, the Teacher, have arisen in the world — a <s>Tathāgata</s>, an <s>Arhat</s> (Worthy One), a Perfectly Awakened One, endowed with knowledge and conduct, a <s>Sugata</s> (Well-Gone One), Knower of the World, unsurpassed charioteer of persons to be tamed, Teacher of gods and humans, a <s>Buddha</s>, a Blessed One. /"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "4 dharmaś ca deśyate aupaśamikaḥ pārinirvāṇikaḥ saṃbodhagāmī suga",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "tapra",
          "segment_number": 37,
          "translated_text": "(Well-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "veditaḥ / yad utāsmiṃ satīdaṃ bhavaty asyotpādād idam utpadyate /",
          "segment_number": 38,
          "translated_text": "Gone One). / That is: when this exists, that comes to be; from the arising of this, that arises. /"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 36,
      "translated_text": "4 And the <s>Dharma</s> (teaching) is taught — leading to pacification, leading to complete <s>nirvāṇa</s>, leading to awakening, proclaimed by the <s>Sugata</s>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "yad utāvidyāpratyayāḥ saṃskārā yāvat samudayo nirodhaś ca bhavati /",
      "segment_number": 39,
      "translated_text": "That is: with ignorance as condition, there are formations; and so on up to arising and cessation. /"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "5 tad idaṃ bhikṣavaḥ sudurlabhadurlabhaṃ yat kadācit karh",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "i",
          "segment_number": 41,
          "translated_text": "an-"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "cid āryāyatane pratyājāti indriyair avikalatā yāvat samudayo nirodhaś ca bhavati /",
          "segment_number": 42,
          "translated_text": "-other, rebirth in a noble realm occurs, completeness of faculties, and so on up to arising and cessation. /"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 40,
      "translated_text": "5 \"This, O <s>bhikṣus</s>, is extremely rare and difficult to obtain — that at some time or"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "6 tasmāt tarhi bhikṣava ātmārthaṃ samanupaśyadbhiḥ pa",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "rārtha",
          "segment_number": 44,
          "translated_text": "the welfare of others,"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "ñ cobhayārthaṃ ca yāvad e",
          "segment_number": 45,
          "translated_text": "and the welfare of both — thus in this manner"
        },
        {
          "tag": "hi",
          "attributes": {
            "rend": "it"
          },
          "text": "vaṃ vo",
          "segment_number": 46,
          "translated_text": "you, O"
        },
        {
          "tag": "text",
          "text": "bhikṣavaḥ śikṣitavyam //",
          "segment_number": 47,
          "translated_text": "<s>bhikṣus</s>, should train. //"
        }
      ],
      "segment_number": 43,
      "translated_text": "6 Therefore, O <s>bhikṣus</s>, seeing your own welfare,"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "7 svāgatasūtraṃ / samāptaḥ //",
      "segment_number": 48,
      "translated_text": "7 The <s>Svāgatasūtra</s> (Sūtra of Welcome) is complete. //"
    }
  ]
}